Huge thanks to Kelly Slater for donating this one-of-a-kind prototype @firewiresurfboards x @slaterdesigns surfboard, the very first production model of the Mike Woo-designed Spaceship model, for the online auction to support Dakota Briley’s recovery. It’s Kelly’s personal board, and he only surfed on it once last week at Cloudbreak in Fiji. As long as I’ve known him, Kelly has always been willing to give back to others and help those in need, despite his busy schedule and all his fame + success. He’s the real deal! 

Mahalo to @peterkingphoto for shooting this clip in Fiji, and for bringing the board back to HI just in time for the auction🚀

This is a once in a lifetime opportunity to own this special board but more importantly to support Dakota and his ohana on his long journey to healing after being hit by a vehicle and sustaining life-threatening injuries. While Dakota is now stable, he has severe spine and brain injuries which requires long-term care and support to cover these extensive medical expenses.

Please click the links in my bio to Dakota’s gofundme and to check out the online auction starting TODAY through Sept 15th and to bid on this surfboard and the many other exciting items that will be for sale, including many surfboards, clothing, jewelry, artwork, gift cards, and much more. 

Mahalo for your support 🙏🏽

